| `change_comments.phrases` | list of strings | `["now", "no longer", "previously", "was changed", "added", "fixed", "used to", "as of", "new:", "changed", "removed", "renamed", "moved"]` | a non-empty list of non-blank strings, matched lowercased | `tests/integration/test_change_comment_gate.py` (`read_lists`); `scripts/jobs/review_docs.py` (`opener_policy`) | Lists the openers that mark a comment reporting a change: a comment that opens a thought and starts with one, followed by a character that is not a letter or digit or by its end, fails the gate test. A thought in a shipped document's prose that opens with one is reported by review_docs as an advisory `OPENER` line, since there it is as often a present claim. Add a phrase when review finds a new opener of that kind. The sibling that fails a compound report anywhere in a shipped document's prose is `doc_drift.forbidden_phrases`. | a phrase in mid-sentence or a change reported in other words, which the heuristic cannot see; document prose inside fences or HTML block types 1 to 7 is exempt, with types 6 and 7 ending before a blank line | always |
